Design of source JSON:
{
  "source_id": "SRC-001",
  "bibkey": "penrose1965",
  "title": "...",
  "authors": ["Roger Penrose"],
  "year": 1965,
  "venue": "Phys. Rev. Lett. 14, 57-59",
  "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.14.57",
  "arxiv_id": null,
  "url": "https://doi.org/...",
  "verification": {
     "method": "primary-page-fetch" | "arxiv-api" | "publisher-page-fetch",
     "fetched_at": "2026-09-11T23:30:00+08:00",
     "http_status": 200,
     "page": "https://...",
     "evidence": "verbatim quoted sentence(s) from the primary source page (abstract or title block)",
     "metadata_confidence": "high|medium|low"
  },
  "status": "verified-primary" | "verified-api" | "unresolved" | "rejected",
  "review_notes": "..."
}
Status semantics:
- verified-primary: fetched the publisher/arXiv abstract page (or API record for the same paper) with title+authors+abstract; metadata matches claim.
- verified-api: arXiv API record only (no HTML page), title/authors/abstract from API.
- unresolved: not yet fetched or conflicting; cannot be cited in accepted entries.
- rejected: fetched source does not support claim, or could not confirm existence (e.g., fabricated).

Theorem JSONL fields (as above). Validation:
- if source status not in {verified-primary, verified-api} → entry cannot be "accepted".
- accepted entries require statement_exact, assumptions, conclusion_type, falsifier list non-empty, class_ids subset of known classes.
- conclusion_type restricted to schema values (theorem, conditional_theorem, stability_result, counterexample, numerical_evidence, formal_model, open_problem) for event compatibility.

Citation audit CSV derived from sources × theorem uses: columns citation_id, bibkey, title, year, venue, used_in, claim_supported, url, verification_method, fetched_at, evidence_excerpt, verdict, reviewer.

Class dossiers generated from theorems grouped by class.

Falsifier matrix generated from theorems.

Unresolved register generated from sources with status unresolved/rejected + theorems provisional.

